      "question": "What are the symptoms of geniculate neuralgia?",
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "Geniculate neuralgia, also known as nervus intermedius neuralgia, is a rare condition causing intense, sharp, and stabbing pain deep inside the ear. This pain can be triggered by activities like touching the ear, yawning, swallowing, or even chewing. Other symptoms may include dizziness, loss of balance, and ringing in the ear (tinnitus).",
          "snippet_highlighted_words": [
            "intense, sharp, and stabbing pain deep inside the ear"
          ],
          "reference_indexes": [
            0,
            1,
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "Key Symptoms:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "snippet": "Sharp, stabbing ear pain: Often described as an \"ice pick\" sensation in the ear.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                1,
                2,
                3,
                6,
                8,
                10
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Electric shock-like pain: The pain can feel like an electrical jolt deep within the ear.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Pain triggered by movement or touch: Activities like chewing, swallowing, or even touching the ear can trigger the pain.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                2,
                11
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Tinnitus: Ringing in the ear can also be a symptom.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Dizziness and loss of balance: These can also occur in some cases.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                1,
                4
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Other facial pain: Some individuals may experience pain in other areas of the face, including the jaw or throat.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                7,
                8,
                13
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Possible triggers: Cold wind, loud noises, and certain movements can trigger the pain.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                9
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "Important Considerations:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "title": "Rarity:",
              "snippet": "Geniculate neuralgia is a rare condition, and its symptoms can sometimes be mistaken for other conditions, like trigeminal neuralgia or cluster headaches.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                9
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Misdiagnosis:",
              "snippet": "Due to the similarity in symptoms, misdiagnosis is common. Patients may be diagnosed with migraines or other conditions before geniculate neuralgia is considered.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                9,
                12
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Seeking medical advice:",
              "snippet": "If you experience persistent or severe ear pain, it's crucial to seek medical attention to determine the cause and receive appropriate treatment.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                1,
